  "description": "SEVXIC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C100 H186 Co6 Gd4 N8 Na2 O44 P6,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.154-3.791 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.94-120.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C100H186Co6Gd4N8Na2O44P6·2MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
